                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "06b14f27-a0a0-3711-9f4e-f6eaca8091b9",
                        "entry_id": "bd2dad83-d7e9-384d-8c2c-280594b1b156",
                        "glosses": [
                            "While young; as a youth."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9128b05e-1ef4-4247-b860-ab95b2a4a943",
                                "sense_id": "06b14f27-a0a0-3711-9f4e-f6eaca8091b9",
                                "text": "And that fresh blood which youngly thou bestow'st"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "605519c7-f4f9-4787-a71a-539598598f48",
                                "sense_id": "06b14f27-a0a0-3711-9f4e-f6eaca8091b9",
                                "text": "In six sexless weeks the least \"good\" of the twenty or so French books I've read is the diary of the youngly-dead Jean-Rene Huguenin (all the rage), because it lacks gossip and carnality, the very stuff of journals."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0a9682bf-09d5-31e8-a1f6-09611215dee8",
                        "entry_id": "bd2dad83-d7e9-384d-8c2c-280594b1b156",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a young or youthful manner; youthfully"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b2ada84-ab49-4e35-865a-ec3b4944c699",
                                "sense_id": "0a9682bf-09d5-31e8-a1f6-09611215dee8",
                                "text": "Refusing to go back to writing things he now thought \"youngly glamorous,\" like Soldiers' Pay, or \"trashily smart,\" like Mosquitoes, he decided to go on even if it meant relinquishing his dream of success."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7e5409f-1844-4eb0-9104-44b03a81f9fb",
                                "sense_id": "0a9682bf-09d5-31e8-a1f6-09611215dee8",
                                "text": "The youngest should speak first, so if I chance In this case to speak youngly, pardon me."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0bfbf496-9f3b-48d0-a4da-a18e32a90edd",
                                "sense_id": "0a9682bf-09d5-31e8-a1f6-09611215dee8",
                                "text": "The youngly born brother made no explanation of his sense of offense other than to go over and give Artie a stolid and resounding blow."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "653f1ec8-c84a-4e60-883f-b8128ae166e4",
                                "sense_id": "0a9682bf-09d5-31e8-a1f6-09611215dee8",
                                "text": "[…]he was also a divine personification, an actual figure, for example sculpted by Skopas (395—350 B.C.), which has been described as a “youngly ripened boy's body.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52add278-f8fd-40bf-b843-50ed0815a8ce",
                                "sense_id": "0a9682bf-09d5-31e8-a1f6-09611215dee8",
                                "text": "Here we sit, the little minister straight from the book, bashful and youngly anxious, and I the Egyptian, not dancing now with rowanberries in her hair, but sadly altered."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
